  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> resistors each of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8486;</mo></math> can be connected in such as to get maximum and minimum equivalent resistance. The ratio of maximum and minimum equivalent resistance will be________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "100",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When all the resistors are connected in series, the total resistance is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>When all the resistors are connected in parallel, the total resistance is</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
